    pilotScope: "A Thai-language enrolment-and-status agent for one named government lending or debt-relief programme across voice and LINE, grounded in the programme eligibility rules and application status system, measured on call abandonment during the announcement surge, branch walk-in deflection and application completion rate.",
    expansion: ["Extend the same agent across all active government programme hotlines as new schemes launch.", "Add proactive document chasing and outbound status updates on restructuring applications.", "Move into everyday retail servicing and MyMo support deflection across the national hotline."],
    stakeholders: ["Executive Vice President, Customer Service / Contact Centre", "Head of Government Programme and Policy Lending", "Chief Information Officer / Head of Digital Banking", "Head of Procurement (state enterprise contracting)", "Data Protection Officer and Head of Compliance"],
    discovery: ["What happens to hotline abandonment rates and branch queues in the week after a government programme is announced, and what is that costing in service failure?", "Can an agentic platform be contracted under an existing systems-integrator framework, or does it require a new tender?", "Where does authoritative programme eligibility logic live today — a system, a circular, or in staff heads?", "What share of hotline calls are pure status enquiries on applications already in progress?"],
    flowTemplate: "inbound-service",
    scenario: "The morning a new government debt-relief scheme is announced, a rural GSB customer asks in Thai whether she qualifies, gets a grounded answer, and books the branch appointment she actually needs.",
